  "body": "Part of #4023. Builds on K0 (`docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md`, PR #4030). This is the first code step. It is delivered on the side branch `side/path-kernel` (AGENTS.md **Side branch**).\n\n## What to do\n\nAdd the crate `camcraft-pathkernel` in `crates/pathkernel/`, as the record defines it.\n\n- The crate depends only on `camcraft-geometry`. `camcraft-motion` depends on it. There is no cycle.\n- Add the stage types of the record: region, guide curves, load control, order, link, entry and exit. Add the law checks as types or traits that the K7 suite (#4027) can call. The types keep open what the record names for the later phases (the work plane, a tool shape that is not only a disc, a guide that is not a plane curve).\n- Add no planner logic in this step. Each stage has its type, its invariants as checked constructors, and unit tests of those invariants.\n- Add the one switch that selects the old or the new planner for the 16 kinds of phase 1. It is read in one place. Its default is the old planner. With the default, the output of each kind is identical to `main`.\n- Add the crate to the gate: the `-p` lists, the lane tables in `xtask/src/lanes.rs` and `xtask/src/plan.rs`, the heavy-lane reach to `motion` and `app`, and the clippy list. The PR body has `Process change: yes`.\n- The record is the dependency decision. Name it in the PR body.\n\n## Pins\n\n- The unit tests of the stage invariants, in the new crate.\n- `switch_default_is_the_old_planner`: with the default, a 2D Offset and a 2D Pocket give the same toolpath as before (compare with the recorded goldens of the branch `issue/3750-shared-ring-set`, commit `9c69f004a`, which the record keeps as the baseline).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --dry-run` on a diff in the new crate lists the new crate's suites, and the `motion` and `app` suites that depend on it.\n\n## Done means\n\nThe crate is on `side/path-kernel`, the switch is at old, the gate knows the crate, and the pins are green. The steps K1 (#4025), K3 (#4026), K7 (#4027) and the kind issues can then start.\n",
